	<!-- A loose custom texture under GUI\SpriteSheets\ is never found by the engine's
	     native resource depot at runtime (Texture.GetFromResource) - confirmed via
	     rgl_log's "Cannot find texture: seljuk_ui_1", logged during the native asset
	     preload pass, before any managed SubModule code even runs. No vanilla
	     AlwaysLoad sprite category ever hits that failure, since their pixels are
	     baked into Native's own compiled ui_charactercreation sheet - loose per-module
	     files aren't a supported input to that pipeline (that requires the official
	     Modding Kit's resource compiler). Instead of a new texture, alias
	     CharacterCreation\Culture\seljuk onto Kara-Khanid (Culture.khuzait)'s existing,
	     already-loaded artwork - Seljuks and Kara-Khanids were both real Turkic
	     steppe dynasties, so the reuse is historically coherent, not just a fallback. -->
